      "text": "Let's break down the problem step by step to find the remainder when the sum \\( 1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259 \\) is divided by 6.\n\n1. **Identify the Pattern:**\n   The sequence of numbers given is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 6\\). We need to determine the number of terms in this sequence.\n\n2. **Find the Number of Terms (n):**\n   We can use the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence:\n   \\[\n   a_n = a + (n-1)d\n   \\]\n   Setting \\(a_n = 259\\),\n   \\[\n   259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\(n\\),\n   \\[\n   259 = 1 + 6n - 6,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   259 = 6n - 5,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   264 = 6n,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   n = 44\n   \\]\n\n3. **Sum of the Sequence:**\n   The sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence can be calculated using the formula:\n   \\[\n   S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l)\n   \\]\n   where \\(l\\) is the last term. Here,\n   \\[\n   l = 259\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   S_{44} = 22 \\cdot 260\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   S_{44} = 5720\n   \\]\n\n4. **Find Remainder When \\(S_{44}\\) is Divided by 6:**\n   Instead of computing the full sum directly, we can use modular arithmetic to find the remainder of \\(5720\\) when divided by \\(6\\). Note that:\n   \\[\n   5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ (quotient)}, \\quad 5720 \\equiv 2 \\text{ (remainder)}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum \\( 1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259 \\) is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
