      "text": "1. Identify the sequence pattern: The sequence gives the following numbers: 1, 7, 13, 19, ..., 253, 259. Observing this, you'll notice that starting from 1, each subsequent number is 6 greater than the previous one.\n  \n2. Derive the sum formula: The sum of the geometric series can be represented as \\(S_n = \\frac{a(1-r^n)}{1-r}\\), where \\(a\\) is the first term, \\(r\\) is the common ratio, and \\(n\\) is the number of terms.\n  \n   - Here, \\(a = 1\\), \\(r = 6\\), and \\(L = 259\\), the last term.\n  \n   Applying the formula, we have \\(S_n = \\frac{1(1-6^n)}{1-6} = \\frac{1-6^n}{-5} = \\frac{6^n - 1}{5}\\).\n\n3. Calculate the sum: We need to find \\(\\frac{6^n-1}{5} \\bmod 6\\). First, observe that \\(6^n \\bmod 6 = 0\\). So, \\(6^n - 1 \\equiv -1 \\equiv 5 \\bmod 6\\) because \\(6 \\equiv -1 \\bmod 6\\).\n   Thus, \\(\\frac{6^n - 1}{5} \\equiv \\frac{5}{5} \\equiv 1 \\bmod 6\\).\n\n4. Remainder analysis: Hence, if \\(a_1, a_2, a_3, \\ldots, a_n\\) represents the sequence and we take \\(a_n \\bmod 6\\), we find that the remainder when \\(a_n\\) is divided by 6 equals 5.\n   Therefore, the remainder when \\(\\frac{1-6^n}{5}\\) is taken modulo 6 is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).",
